# The fortune teller trades in silver and silence: every question
# gets a finger to her lips, but the silver museum key on her palm
# buys the reading. Time, Art or Force -- Time, "As it was". The
# glass pendant she leaves on the table is the museum's missing
# ping-pong-ball-sized hoop-piece (the clock glass never fit --
# "a little too big", a silent failure the original session
# carried for four hundred lines) AND the doorway to the visions:
# it slings itself around your neck and your own hand touches the
# disc, unasked.
east
give key to teller
time
think about time
look
